WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.810
I'm a historian of policy.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.850
I study the plans an institution quietly stops pursuing.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:13.890
Dr Marek Solheim is Deputy Convenor of the Horizon Register at Slop University.

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:17.440
Very few plans are ever formally retired.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.490
Most are simply left to lapse.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:23.680
A café loyalty account, still counted as active.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:27.050
An exam-hall flag, ticked as resolved.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.890
A laundromat sign that says back soon.

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.870
Colleagues across the University build on that work.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.860
His h-index is twenty-six,

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.475
the second-highest in the School of Emergent Priorities.

00:00:38.725 --> 00:00:41.675
And he's been cited nine hundred and forty-six times.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.695
Every plan gets a launch.

00:00:44.945 --> 00:00:46.985
I'd like its ending written down, too.

00:00:47.985 --> 00:00:49.657
Explore his research on our website,

00:00:49.807 --> 00:00:51.087
keep up with us on Bluesky,

00:00:51.237 --> 00:00:51.957
or email us.
